description.narrative:
This project was implement 1 July 2021 to 31 December 2022 and was subsequently heavily impacted by the full-scale Russian invasion of Ukraine.

- Recommendations for mainstreaming Nature-based Solutions into sectoral policies (forest, water management, agriculture and environmental sphere) for climate adaptation and post-war recovery were developed through a series of workshops, which ensured support by key stakeholders.

- The Ukrainian public and experts were informed about best practices and approaches to implement Nature-based Solutions through the first Ukrainian-language Nature-based Solutions platform (www.nbs.wwf.ua), a website that will continue to server as source of information for those responsible for strategic planning and practical implementation of Nature-based Solutions, serving learning and knowledge exchange;

- Young people were inspired and engaged, equipped with knowledge and capacitated to act through a youth-oriented leadership programme (for 14 young people) and an open training course;

- Three local CSOs were engaged and capacitated to implement Nature-based Solutions through a small grants programme. The programme brought together non-governmental organisations and executive authorities of local communities to mainstream Nature-based Solutions into local strategic development and restoration plans and proved that there is need and interest at local level in learning about and implementing Nature-based Solutions;

- Representatives of state executive authorities increased their knowledge about Nature-based Solutions and best practice implementation by actively participating in a study tour to Bavaria, Germany and/or joining the Final Conference in Brussels, where they could interact with representatives of the EU Commission,

- Staff of WWF-Ukraine, CSO participants of the small grants programme and the national expert community involved in the project improved their knowledge and skills regarding integrating gender and human rights-based approaches into environmental activities by attending training sessions organized by WWF-Sweden

- The topic of Nature-based Solutions implementation for the post-war recovery of Ukraine was raised to the attention of stakeholders. It is popularised to such an extent that leading media have started communicating about Nature-based Solutions.
